# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which converts
# LF to CRLF on checkout. For shell scripts that is not cosmetic: Git Bash
# tolerates a CRLF script, but real Linux bash does not, and this project
# has a WSL Debian install one command away. Measured, not assumed —
# `wsl bash -n scripts/flash-dfu.sh` on the CRLF working copy gave:
#
#     syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# while the same file ran fine under Git Bash. So the breakage is silent
# until someone runs a script from WSL or CI, which is exactly when they
# least want to be debugging line endings.
#
# Scoped to the two extensions that care rather than a blanket
# `* text=auto`, which would renormalise every file in the repo and bury a
# real change in a whitespace diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
